    "custom_liquid_VDPAtL": {
      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "{% if template.name == 'product' %}\n <section id=\"faq-section\" class=\"faq-container\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-title\">\n    <h2 id=\"faq-title\" class=\"faq-title\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">What is the difference between nearsighted and farsighted lenses?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p><strong>Nearsighted (Myopia) lenses:</strong> Negative SPH values (example: -2.50) to help you see clearly at distance.</p>\n        <p><strong>Farsighted (Hyperopia) lenses:</strong> Positive SPH values (example: +2.50) to help with close-up vision.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">How do I find the sphere (SPH) value on my prescription?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>Look for the column labelled <strong>SPH</strong> or <strong>Sphere</strong>. It can also be labelled <strong>Power</strong> or <strong>PWR</strong>. A minus sign (-) is nearsighted. A plus sign (+) is farsighted.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">How should I adjust my prescription for clear vision underwater?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p><strong>Underwater adjustment:</strong> For most people, choosing a lens that is <strong>0.50 diopters weaker</strong> (towards zero) than your normal SPH gives the best comfort and clarity underwater.</p>\n        <p><strong>Why:</strong> Water creates natural magnification, and mask lenses sit further from your eyes than glasses. Reducing by 0.50 helps keep vision feeling natural and comfortable underwater.</p>\n        <p><strong>Examples:</strong> If your SPH is -2.25, choose -2.00. If your SPH is -2.75, choose -2.50.</p>\n        <p>Our lenses are available in <strong>0.50 increments</strong>, so choose the closest available option.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">I have astigmatism (CYL). What should I choose?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>Our lenses are sphere only, meaning they correct SPH but not CYL directly. You can still see a significant improvement. Use your SPH for each eye, then adjust based on your CYL value and sign.</p>\n\n        <p><strong>Important:</strong> The + or − sign on your CYL matters. Check your prescription slip for the sign next to your CYL value.</p>\n\n        <p><strong>Nearsighted (Minus −) lenses</strong></p>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>CYL 0.00 to 0.75:</strong> Go <strong>0.50 weaker</strong> than your SPH (closer to zero). The CYL sign has little impact at this level.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 1.00 to 1.75 with minus CYL (−):</strong> Stay close to your SPH. You can go up to 0.50 stronger (further from zero) or up to 0.50 weaker (closer to zero).</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 1.00 to 1.75 with plus CYL (+):</strong> Stay close to your SPH. You can go up to 0.50 weaker (closer to zero) or stay at SPH.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 2.00 to 3.00 with minus CYL (−):</strong> Stay exactly at your SPH. Only go 0.50 stronger if you specifically want sharper detail.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 2.00 to 3.00 with plus CYL (+):</strong> Stay exactly at your SPH. Do not go weaker.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 3.25+ with minus CYL (−):</strong> Move slightly toward stronger correction, rounded to the nearest 0.50 step.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 3.25+ with plus CYL (+):</strong> Move slightly toward weaker correction, rounded to the nearest 0.50 step.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <p><strong>Special case:</strong> If your SPH is −0.50 or −0.75 and CYL is 2.50 or higher, start at −1.00.</p>\n\n        <p><strong>Farsighted (Plus +) lenses</strong></p>\n        <p>Our farsighted lenses come in whole steps only: <strong>+1.00, +2.00, +3.00, +4.00, +5.00</strong>.</p>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>CYL 0.00 to 0.75:</strong> Round to the nearest whole number toward zero.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 1.00 to 1.75 with minus CYL (−):</strong> Round to nearest whole number, or one step stronger for sharper detail.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 1.00 to 1.75 with plus CYL (+):</strong> Round down to the nearest whole number.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 2.00 to 3.00:</strong> Stay at your SPH rounded to the nearest whole number.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 3.25+ with minus CYL (−):</strong> Move toward stronger correction, round to nearest whole number.</li>\n          <li><strong>CYL 3.25+ with plus CYL (+):</strong> Move toward weaker correction, round to nearest whole number.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <p><strong>Special case:</strong> If your SPH is +0.50 or +0.75, start at +1.00 regardless of CYL.</p>\n\n        <p>Use our <a href=\"https://oceansoptics.com/pages/lens-calculator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Underwater Lens Calculator</a> for an instant recommendation, or see our full guide: <a href=\"https://oceansoptics.com/pages/choosing-prescription-snorkel-mask-lenses-with-astigmatism\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Choosing prescription snorkel mask lenses with astigmatism</a>.</p>\n\n        <p>If you are unsure, upload your prescription and we will check your selection for you.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">I can't find my lens strength in the dropdown. What should I do?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>The dropdown shows all strengths available for that specific mask. If your exact number is not listed, choose the closest available option using the guidance above.</p>\n        <p>If you want us to confirm the best match, upload your prescription on the product page or email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@oceansoptics.com\">info@oceansoptics.com</a>.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">Can I choose different lens strengths for each eye?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>Yes. You can select different strengths for left and right eye. You can mix and match any combination available in the dropdown menu.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">How do I upload my prescription during checkout?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>On the product page you can optionally upload your prescription so we can check your selection before we build it. You can also leave a note in the cart, or email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@oceansoptics.com\">info@oceansoptics.com</a>.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">How do I stop my mask from fogging?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>A simple method is the toothpaste trick. Rub a small amount of toothpaste on the <strong>inside</strong> of each lens using circular motions for a few minutes, then rinse thoroughly. Do this before your first use and repeat if needed.</p>\n        <p>Before each session, you can also use a tiny amount of <strong>baby shampoo</strong> or <strong>dish soap</strong> mixed with water. Rub a thin film on the inside of the lens, then lightly rinse so a fine layer remains.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">Do you have a guide to help me use my mask properly?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>Yes. Here is our Mask 101 guide: <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0798/8055/2781/files/Mask_101.pdf?v=1728895468\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open Mask 101 (PDF)</a>.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">What happens if I accidentally choose the wrong lens strength?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>Message us as soon as possible. If the order has not entered the build or shipping stage yet, we can usually update the lens selection.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">Are your lenses safe for both snorkeling and scuba diving?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>Yes. Our lenses are HD tempered glass and are suitable for snorkeling and scuba diving up to 100 ft (30 m).</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">How long does delivery take, and can I track my order?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p>Most orders arrive in <strong>5 to 10 days</strong>, but we recommend allowing up to <strong>14 days</strong> to be safe. You will receive a tracking number by email once your order ships.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <details class=\"faq-item\">\n      <summary class=\"faq-question\">What is your return or exchange policy for prescription masks?</summary>\n      <div class=\"faq-answer\">\n        <p><strong>Your satisfaction, guaranteed.</strong><br>\n        You have 30 days from delivery to request a return, as long as the item is unworn, unused, with tags, and in original packaging. For full details, visit our <a href=\"https://oceansoptics.com/pages/returns-and-warranty\">Return Policy</a>.</p>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n  </section>\n\n  <script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n    {\n      \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n      \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n      \"mainEntity\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What is the difference between nearsighted and farsighted lenses?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Nearsighted (myopia) lenses use negative SPH values to correct distance vision. Farsighted (hyperopia) lenses use positive SPH values to help with close-up vision.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How do I find the sphere (SPH) value on my prescription?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Look for SPH or Sphere. It can also be labelled Power or PWR. A minus sign (-) is nearsighted and a plus sign (+) is farsighted.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How should I adjust my prescription for clear vision underwater?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"For most people, choose 0.50 diopters weaker (towards zero) than your normal SPH, then select the closest available 0.50 step.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"I have astigmatism (CYL). What should I choose?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Use your SPH for each eye. The + or minus sign on your CYL matters. Nearsighted: CYL 0.00 to 0.75 go 0.50 weaker. CYL 1.00 to 1.75 minus CYL stay close to SPH up to 0.50 either direction. CYL 1.00 to 1.75 plus CYL stay at SPH or 0.50 weaker. CYL 2.00+ minus CYL stay at SPH. CYL 2.00+ plus CYL stay at SPH. CYL 3.25+ nudges toward SE. Farsighted lenses come in whole steps +1 to +5. Special case: SPH -0.50 or -0.75 with CYL 2.50+ start at -1.00. SPH +0.50 or +0.75 start at +1.00.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"I can't find my lens strength in the dropdown. What should I do?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Choose the closest available option. Upload your prescription or email info@oceansoptics.com if you want us to confirm the best match.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can I choose different lens strengths for each eye?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes. You can select different strengths for left and right eye and mix and match any combination available in the dropdown.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How do I upload my prescription during checkout?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"On the product page you can optionally upload your prescription. You can also leave a note in the cart or email info@oceansoptics.com.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How do I stop my mask from fogging?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Try the toothpaste trick: rub a small amount on the inside of each lens in circular motions, then rinse. Before each session use a tiny amount of baby shampoo or dish soap, rub a thin film on the lens, then lightly rinse.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Do you have a guide to help me use my mask properly?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes. Mask 101 guide: https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0798/8055/2781/files/Mask_101.pdf?v=1728895468\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What happens if I accidentally choose the wrong lens strength?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Message us as soon as possible. If the order has not entered the build or shipping stage yet, we can usually update the lens selection.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Are your lenses safe for both snorkeling and scuba diving?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes. Lenses are HD tempered glass and suitable for snorkeling and scuba diving up to 100 ft (30 m).\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"How long does delivery take, and can I track my order?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Most orders arrive in 5 to 10 days, but allow up to 14 days to be safe. Tracking is provided by email once shipped.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What is your return or exchange policy for prescription masks?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"You have 30 days from delivery to request a return as long as the item is unworn, unused, with tags, and in original packaging.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  </script>\n\n  <style>\n    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }\n\n    .faq-container {\n      max-width: 700px;\n      margin: 20px auto;\n      padding: 20px;\n      border-top: 1px solid #023059;\n      font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;\n    }\n\n    .faq-title {\n      font-size: 26px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #023059;\n      text-align: center;\n      margin-bottom: 20px;\n    }\n\n    .faq-item {\n      border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\n      margin-bottom: 6px;\n    }\n\n    .faq-question {\n      font-size: 16px;\n      background-color: #ffffff;\n      color: #023059;\n      padding: 14px 16px;\n      cursor: pointer;\n      border: 1px solid #023059;\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      margin: 0;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      list-style: none;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      gap: 10px;\n      transition: background-color 0.2s ease;\n    }\n\n    .faq-question:hover {\n      background-color: #f